// The per-process address spaces (T6.2): every user process runs on
// its own Sv39 table, built at spawn — the image's segments (code RX,
// data RW, a shared boundary page where the ELF's segments meet inside
// one 4 KiB page, the union of the two), the process's own stack block
// and arena run, the user cells page, each with U, and the kernel's
// whole high half beside them with no U (sv39.map_kernel) — the boot
// pass's trap page (T6.3) included, rw without U. U-mode's
// world is exactly those pages: its code, its image's data (the passes
// of one image share it — a spawned pass re-enters the top level and
// finds the tokens the parent poked, the spawn semantics since T4.4),
// its own stack and arena, the cells the trap shim hands the arena
// through — and nothing else. Every kernel byte is mapped in the same
// table without U: the kernel runs on whichever table satp names, and
// a trap out of a pass finds its own world; U-mode reaching for any of
// it is a page fault the shim kills the pass for (T6.4's work, the
// fault route already takes any exception). The window's two gigapages
// with U are gone: the per-process tables are what close it.
//
// The untyped-memory discipline as everywhere: Int64 addresses,
// peek/poke, bit masks, every def a fully typed native body — the
// build runs inside emo_user_spawn's masked region and the switch
// inside the pick's, so nothing here may allocate.
//
// The runtime reaches this module through the hook words its stub
// parks, the block hooks' pattern: emo_space_build_hook (the build,
// called at the end of emo_user_spawn with the child's slot),
// emo_space_hook (the resolve, called by the pick with the incoming
// slot's word and answered the physical root to install — or -1 when
// satp already names it), and emo_space_write_hook (the write itself,
// parked at sv39.S's emo_os_satp_switch). A slot word of 0 means the
// kernel's own table: every green process's word, the kernel root's
// until the boot pass adopts its own. The boot pass's table is built
// by the loader (user.emo) at stage time and adopted by the kernel's
// enter shim (trap.S) through adopt before the first sret into
// U-mode, so the boot pass's own word is in its slot before its first
// trap can preempt it.

const koff = -274877906944 // 0xFFFFFFC000000000: the high half's base

// The Sv39 page: the kernel root's kernel address (sv39.emo wrote it
// at boot), and the current cell — the physical root satp names right
// now, the switch's cache: resolve answers -1 when the incoming word
// resolves to what is already installed, so the kernel's processes
// switching among themselves fence nothing.
const root_cell = koff + 0x87004000
const current_cell = koff + 0x87004010

// The handoff page: the segment table the loader parked (the gate's
// constants). The staged space cell the boot pass's table rides in
// lives here too — the loader writes it, the enter shim reads it —
// but through user.emo's own constants.
const seg_count_addr = koff + 0x87002018
const seg_table = koff + 0x87002020

// The user cells page (T5.1): the user stub parks the addresses of
// its root slot's arena words here; every trap out of a pass and every
// resume into one crosses these cells, so every user table carries
// them, with U — the user stub writes them at the boot pass's entry.
const cells_page = 0x87fff000

// The boot pass's trap page (T6.3): the fixed page under the cells
// page, the one memory the boot pass's frame parks in — the image's
// stack is the stub's own and the heap is live data, so the page is
// the scratch that belongs to no pass's execution. Mapped rw without U
// into every table (the trampoline stores through the pass's own
// before the swap; the low window covers the kernel-side accesses), so
// U-mode cannot touch it and a wild store there is the fault the shim
// kills the pass for.
const boot_trap_page = 0x87ffe000

// The ELF's p_flags (X=1, W=2, R=4), as the loader parked them, and
// the entry bits this module writes: the permissions translated, U
// on every leaf, V and A and D as sv39.map sets them.
const flag_x = 1
const flag_w = 2
const flag_r = 4
const pte_v = 1
const pte_r = 2
const pte_w = 4
const pte_x = 8
const pte_u = 16
const pte_a = 64
const pte_d = 128
const rwu = pte_r | pte_w | pte_u
const rw = pte_r | pte_w
const page = 4096
const block = 65536

// The slot words the build reads: the arena's base at 880 (the run's
// first block, a kernel address) and the arena's end at 584 (the run's
// one-past end — between them the whole run the spawn claimed, the
// length never this module's guess), the stack block at 864 (its
// physical base — the pass runs on the identity alias of its block),
// and the space word at 872 the build answers into (the stride 888).
const slot_arena_base = 880
const slot_arena_end = 584
const slot_stack = 864
const slot_space = 872

// The screen carve's grant (T8.2): the cell on the handoff page the
// process service pokes with the carve's kernel address when the spawn
// it is serving is the machine's full-screen pass — the screen token's
// other half, read at the spawn because the carve's mapping must exist
// before the child's first store. The build consumes it: the cell is
// zero again after the one build that mapped the carve, and a spawn
// without the grant builds a table that maps none of it. The mapping
// is the identity of the carve's physical addresses — RW with U,
// megapages — both ends 2 MiB-aligned, and no block of the allocator's
// region can sit there (the carve is the region's exclusion,
// frames.emo's), so the two megapage leaves cost no table beyond the
// entries the low half's middle already carries. The cell sits past
// the write's staging area (gate.emo's stage_buf, the handoff page's
// free tail) — the first boot caught the collision: user bytes landed
// in the cell and the build mapped a phantom grant, the range check
// the loud end.
const screen_pending = koff + 0x870029e0
const screen_size = 0x400000 // 4 MiB, frames.emo's carve

// The exec's pending record (emo-desktop A11.1): the cell the process
// service pokes with the image record's address right before the spawn
// that starts it — the grant's shape again, the record's mapping
// existing before the child's first fetch. The build consumes it into
// the child's own image cell (one write per pid ever, the pid already
// dressed in the slot), and the table is built off that image's own
// segments — the per-image half, the boot image's global table the
// zero cell's answer. The record's tail word (+224, exec.emo's
// record_page) is the image's private handoff page (emo-desktop
// A11.2): the frame the transaction took, the build maps it at the
// cells page's vaddr in the child's table and parks the child's arena
// values on it — the classic cells page stays the boot image's, its
// stub's parks never stolen, and two images hand their arenas side by
// side, each through its own page.
const exec_pending = koff + 0x8700c000 + 3904
const img_for = koff + 0x8700c000
const record_page = 224

// One 4 KiB page into a user table, unioning with what is there: the
// image's segments share their boundary page (the text's last page
// holds the data's first bytes in this ELF's layout), so a page the
// walk already mapped gets its permissions OR'd in — same physical
// page or the loud end — and a fresh one is written leaf-complete.
// Everything else about the mapping is sv39.map's strictness; the
// union is what makes an unaligned segment pair map at all.
def map_page(root Int64, va Int64, pa Int64, flags Int64) Void {
  var at = sv39.slot_of(root, va, 0)
  var e = peek64(at)
  if (e & pte_v) != 0 {
    if sv39.pte_pa(e) != pa {
      sv39.die("sv39: two segments claim one page differently")
    }
    poke64(at, e | flags)
  } else {
    poke64(at, sv39.pte_of(pa, flags | pte_v | pte_a | pte_d))
  }
}

// The user's half of a table: the kernel's half and the boot pass's
// trap page — everything but the image's segments and the handoff
// page, the two builders' shared part. One helper for the three
// builders — the boot pass's (user.emo's stage, which knows the
// segments before anything spawns), each spawned pass's (build, off
// the boot image's global table), and an exec's child's (build, off
// the child's own image's record). The cells page's vaddr is each
// builder's own: the boot image's table maps the classic cells page
// (its stub's parks — the identity the kernel's low window reads), an
// exec'd image's maps its private handoff page (image_base's, the
// frame the record names).
def base_common(root Int64) Void {
  sv39.map_kernel(root, false)
  map_page(root, boot_trap_page, boot_trap_page, rw)
}

// The boot image's segments: the global table the loader parked (the
// gate's constants), each page at the identity of its address — the
// image was copied to its link addresses at stage time, and every pass
// of the boot image shares those physical pages.
def base(root Int64) Void {
  base_common(root)
  map_page(root, cells_page, cells_page, rwu)
  var n = peek64(seg_count_addr)
  var i = 0
  while i < n {
    var slot = seg_table + (i * 24)
    var start = peek64(slot)
    var endp = peek64(slot + 8)
    var pf = peek64(slot + 16)
    var flags = seg_flags(pf)
    var va = (start / page) * page
    while va < endp {
      map_page(root, va, va, flags)
      va = va + page
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
}

// The ELF's p_flags translated to the PTE's permission bits, U on top:
// code RX, data RW — and where one page carries both, both.
def seg_flags(pf Int64) Int64 {
  var flags = 0
  if (pf & flag_r) != 0 {
    flags = flags | pte_r
  }
  if (pf & flag_w) != 0 {
    flags = flags | pte_w
  }
  if (pf & flag_x) != 0 {
    flags = flags | pte_x
  }
  return flags | pte_u
}

// An exec'd image's segments (emo-desktop A11.1): the record the
// loader filled — the segment rows in the handoff table's own shape,
// the run's physical base and length beside them. Each page maps at
// the run's identity of its offset: the image's first page sits at the
// run's base, every link address at the base plus its offset — the
// per-image segment table, each image's world its own physical pages
// at the addresses it was linked to. The count word doubles as the
// live flag; the record the caller names was consumed from the
// pending cell, and the pid's image cell was written beside it (one
// write per pid ever — the gate's checks and the death's walk read
// it).
def image_base(root Int64, rec Int64) Void {
  base_common(root)
  var n = peek64(rec)
  var floor = (peek64(rec + 8) / page) * page
  var run_base = peek64(rec + 208)
  var i = 0
  while i < n {
    var slot = rec + 8 + (i * 24)
    var start = peek64(slot)
    var endp = peek64(slot + 8)
    var flags = seg_flags(peek64(slot + 16))
    var va = (start / page) * page
    while va < endp {
      map_page(root, va, run_base + (va - floor), flags)
      va = va + page
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  // the private handoff page (emo-desktop A11.2): the cells page's
  // vaddr maps the image's own frame — the stub's parks, the delta the
  // transaction poked, the arena values the build parks, every cell
  // the stub and the runtime's init read, land here and nowhere else.
  // The record's word is the kernel's alias; the PTE takes the
  // physical.
  map_page(root, cells_page, sv39.pa_of(peek64(rec + record_page)), rwu)
}

// The boot pass's adoption: its root's physical address, into the
// switch's cache — the enter shim (trap.S) calls this before its own
// satp_switch, so the cache stays true about what satp holds and the
// first resolve neither skips a needed write nor repeats the boot's.
def adopt(root_pa Int64) Void {
  poke64(current_cell, root_pa)
}

// The spawned pass's table, built at spawn: the runtime's hook, called
// at the end of emo_user_spawn with the child's slot — every word the
// build needs is already in it. The kernel's half, the image's
// segments, the cells page (base), then the process's own: its stack
// block, and its arena whole — every block of the run from the base at
// 880 up to the end at 584 (T8.9), each 4 KiB at the identity of its
// physical address, RW with U. The root's physical address goes into
// the slot's space word — what the switch resolves on every pick.
// Frame exhaustion is the loud end, as the arena carve's is: the
// process table's ceiling in memory.
def build(slot Int64) Void {
  var root = frames.frame_take()
  if root == 0 {
    sv39.die("sv39: no frame left for a process table")
  }
  sv39.clear(root)
  // The exec's pending record (emo-desktop A11.1): the one spawn that
  // starts a disk ELF carries its record, and this build is the one
  // consumer — the record goes into the child's own image cell, the
  // table built off the image's own segments. Every other spawn finds
  // the cell zero and builds off the boot image's global table, the
  // shape every pass has carried since T6.2.
  var rec = peek64(exec_pending)
  if rec != 0 {
    poke64(exec_pending, 0)
    var pid = peek64(slot + 8)
    if pid < 256 {
      poke64(img_for + pid * 8, rec)
    }
    // the child's arena crosses as values on its own private page
    // (emo-desktop A11.2): the slot's own run, the cursor and end the
    // spawn dressed, physical — the identities the image's own table
    // maps — read here, after the dress, by the runtime's init (the
    // delta word its tell). The record's page word is the kernel's
    // alias, as the allocator answered it.
    var hp = peek64(rec + record_page)
    poke64(hp + 0x70, sv39.pa_of(peek64(slot + slot_arena_base)))
    poke64(hp + 0x78, sv39.pa_of(peek64(slot + slot_arena_end)))
    image_base(root, rec)
  } else {
    base(root)
  }
  var stack = peek64(slot + slot_stack)
  var va = stack
  var top = stack + block
  while va < top {
    map_page(root, va, va, rwu)
    va = va + page
  }
  var arena = sv39.pa_of(peek64(slot + slot_arena_base))
  top = sv39.pa_of(peek64(slot + slot_arena_end))
  va = arena
  while va < top {
    map_page(root, va, va, rwu)
    va = va + page
  }
  // The screen carve's grant (T8.2): the service poked the cell before
  // the spawn; this build is the one consumer. The carve maps at the
  // identity of its physical addresses — the pass paints it where the
  // device will scan it out of — RW with U, megapages both ends.
  var screen = peek64(screen_pending)
  if screen != 0 {
    poke64(screen_pending, 0)
    var spa = sv39.pa_of(screen)
    sv39.map_range(root, spa, spa, screen_size, rwu)
  }
  poke64(slot + slot_space, sv39.pa_of(root))
}

// The switch's resolve: the incoming slot's word to the physical root
// satp should name — 0 means the kernel's own table, every green
// process's answer — or -1 when that is already installed, the cache
// hit that keeps the kernel's processes switching among themselves
// without a fence. A miss is recorded before the answer: the caller's
// write is the next thing that happens, and a resolve whose write was
// skipped would leave the cache lying about satp.
def switch(w Int64) Int64 {
  var target = w
  if w == 0 {
    target = sv39.pa_of(peek64(root_cell))
  }
  if target == peek64(current_cell) {
    return -1
  }
  poke64(current_cell, target)
  return target
}

// A window buffer's run, mapped into its owner's table after the spawn
// (T8.5) — the incremental half of the build: a table that exists
// grows a mapping the way the spawn's built one. The run maps at the
// identity of its physical addresses, RW with U — the same discipline
// the stack and the arena blocks ride — megapages wherever the
// alignment gives them (map_range's rule). The root arrives physical
// (the gate stages the caller's space word into the request, the
// shim's staging read inside the caller's own trap); the walk rides
// the kernel's aliases of the table frames, and the new entries are
// whole words the hardware walk either misses or sees complete. The
// fence is the live table's own discipline — the spawn's build wrote
// a table no satp named yet, and this one is installed: the sfence
// after the last entry is what makes the mapping visible to the walks
// the owner's next stores take.
def map_run(root_pa Int64, base_pa Int64, len Int64) Void {
  var root = sv39.va_of(root_pa)
  sv39.map_range(root, base_pa, base_pa, len, rwu)
  sfence()
}
